WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.620
Charlotte, I would like to endorse you to be the next president of the United States.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.420
Oh my god.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.620
You've been a great secretary.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.820
Of State.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.760
Which state again?

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.320
All of them.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.300
Is that the Secretary of State looking at us?

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.220
I kind of know her.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.360
It's like kind of knowing a mermaid.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:26.360
Do you tell people that?

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.480
She probably doesn't remember who I am.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.400
Secretary Field would like to speak with you.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.540
With me?

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.600
I can't shake this feeling that we know each other.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.100
We do!

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:34.600
We do?

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.840
Picture me, I guess, maybe like 20 years younger, but like this.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:38.800
Flarsky?

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:39.600
Yeah.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.600
What are you doing these days?

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.300
I'm a journalist.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:45.180
You're a great writer, but, sometimes you're a little too much.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.600
I don't think I am too much! I actually think I'm the perfect, right, portion.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.240
It's really nice to see you again.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:50.740
Woah!

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.360
*screaming*

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.360
Cracker down!

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.100
I'm okay!

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.400
Okay, did he just call me a cracker?

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.480
What is the relationship exactly?

00:00:59.480 --> 00:00:59.980
*chuckles*

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.360
It's to babysit for him.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.620
You babysat for him?

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.100
Wow. Time has not been kind.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.160
I need some writers to punch up my speeches.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.020
Fred's writing is really good and he knows me.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.120
Oh, I feel so scared.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.940
In order to write better for you, I should kind of get to know you better... if you have a minute.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.060
I actually have seven.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.120
Seven minutes in heaven.

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:21.480
*chuckles*

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.220
What is your favourite book as a kid?

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.160
The Velveteen Rabbit.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:25.720
Favourite song?

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.240
'Must have been loved' by Roxette.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.320
Most embarrassing moment?

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.560
I don't know embarrass that easily.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.620
I don't either, really.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.320
What's your favourite sexual position?

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.760
Normal, front-facing, normal.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.820
What kind of question is that?

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:35.720
That's all it took, look at you!

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.520
*stuttering* What's your favourite sexual position?

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.500
Don't be gross, alright?

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:40.780
Do a date.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.920
I mean, who wants to follow me around the world and hope I have five minutes to be affectionate?

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:45.420
Yeah.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:49.560
We did almost just die.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.740
We actually did almost die.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.440
We need to move you.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.600
Thank you, Agent M.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:01.080
It's 'Pretty Woman', but she's Richard Gere and you're Julia Roberts.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.220
Honestly, this has been the best few weeks of my entire life.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.480
We asked a thousand constituents how they would feel if Kate Middleton-

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:11.540
I see where you're going with this.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.580
-were to start dating Danny DeVito.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.520
Pretty negative reaction.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.720
The last time you got high was on a *inaudible* concert?

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.340
We have a situation.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:28.040
Huh?

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.180
I'm in so much trouble.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.880
What's happened? Are they out of water?

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.720
*laughing*

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:37.540
Wow, he's so bendy, huh?

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:38.800
Ooh!

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:39.660
Ouch!

